WEBVTT

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:18.740
On a cold winter day, 
nothing is better

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:18.740
than being in a warm 
room with some oden.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:17.660
On a cold winter day, nothing is better 
than being in a warm room with some oden.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:22.750
<b>Episode 25</b>

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:22.750
<b>Oden with the
 White Tiger</b>

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.890
Delicious

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.890
<b>Fish 
Roll</b>

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:26.000
<b>SO MUCH〜</b>

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:25.990
Wow, what are you doing with all this?

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:29.310
I thought I'd make some oden, 
since it's so cold.

00:00:29.310 --> 00:00:30.800
Let's eat it with everyone when it's done.

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:33.550
You're going to make it, Dazai-san?

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:35.760
I'll call Yosano-sensei.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.780
<b>If you nearly die,
 I'll fix you right up ♡</b>

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.950
<i>If you nearly die, I'll fix you right up ♡</i>

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.040
Are you saying my cooking is near-fatal?

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.020
How rude.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:42.150
Now, then...

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.350
What should I do?

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:48.900
<b>Worry</b>

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:48.820
Do you even know how 
to make oden, Dazai-san?

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:50.980
Convenience store. Be right back.

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:53.020
You're trying to buy some, aren't you?!

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.880
To be honest, I gathered 
everything on a whim.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.870
I don't cook very much.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:00.040
I don't know how to make oden, either.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:02.930
I know. Let's ask Kunikida-kun.

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:05.160
Kunikida-san's out working right now.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.540
All good!

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:09.030
I heard our company's in danger!

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.480
<i>Poor guy.</i>

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:14.990
How to make oden?

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:16.060
I'm so sorry!

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:17.020
The broth!

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:18.500
Have you made the broth yet?

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:19.380
That's what you're mad about?

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:22.260
Start with the stuff that takes 
longer to absorb flavor.

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:24.640
Freeze the daikon first 
to make it soak up more.

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.140
<i>Now he's making oden...</i>

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:28.220
<i>I'm scared of how knowledgeable he is.</i>

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:30.570
I'll be the tasting expert.

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:33.600
There, done.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:41.780
Onii-sama must get in all sorts 
of trouble when I'm not around.

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:46.060
I want to be more use 
to him when I'm with him.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:47.640
Whatever shall I do?

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:51.390
Naomi...

00:01:51.390 --> 00:01:52.950
What's gotten into you?

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:56.660
I'm in ecstasy, being so close to you 
and becoming your arms and legs.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:58.840
I shall feed you now.

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:00.040
N-Naomi-san...

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:01.670
Here, Onii-sama.

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:03.670
Say "ah."

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:04.960
Hot!

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:06.300
I knew it!

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.750
I knew this would happen!

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:10.050
Let's eat.

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:10.930
Let's eat.

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:16.500
This is your first time eating 
oden, huh, Kyouka-chan?

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:17.270
Yeah.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:18.780
I'll get you some.

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:20.050
What do you want?

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:21.660
Tofu.

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:24.700
Oh, this is a hanpen.

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:26.190
H-Hanpen?!

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:28.850
What's that?

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:30.120
Try it.

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:32.170
Hot!

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:34.560
It's good, though.

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:35.450
I'm glad.

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:37.160
Huh?

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:39.330
The pot's full of mochi.

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:41.670
Are you even supposed
 to put mochi in oden?

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:43.090
Oh, that?

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:44.100
<b>Schwing</b>

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:46.410
Yosano-sensei disassembled 
the mochi kinchaku.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.410
I'll handle this!

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:48.850
After all the effort Kunikida-san 
put into wrapping them?!

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:51.940
And Rampo-san eats the fried 
tofu skins and kanpyo.

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:53.110
Yum.

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:54.480
Why are you eating just the outsides?

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.940
I don't want the mochi. 
It doesn't taste like anything.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.000
What a waste!

00:02:58.290 --> 00:02:59.870
You all seem to be having fun.

00:02:59.870 --> 00:03:00.960
President.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:03.850
Rampo can be unpredictable,

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.990
but I hope you afford him the same 
respect as any other Agency member.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:07.820
Yes, of course, sir.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:10.790
He's a good person at heart.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:14.090
That's taking things too far, Rampo-san!

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:15.250
<b>Please don't do this</b>

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:17.400
He's not a bad person...

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.750
You seem really strained, President.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.120
He's not a bad person.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:23.810
Everyone's enjoying the oden, huh?

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:26.360
You haven't had any, Dazai-san.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:27.650
This was your idea.

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:32.190
I'm content just seeing 
everyone eat it so happily.

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:33.190
Burp.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:36.640
<i>Ah, he's been taste-testing like crazy.</i>

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:39.800
Burp.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:47.530
<b>Dazai Osamu-style
 Oden With A 
Twist Recipe</b>

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:47.530
<b>1. Have Nakajima Atsushi
 buy the ingredients</b>

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:47.530
<b>2. Call Kunikida Doppo</b>

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:51.540
<b>Episode 26</b>

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:51.540
<b>Elevator Panic</b>

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:56.540
<b>It's a sale!
 It's a bargain!</b>

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:56.540
<b>Sky Restaurant 
10th Floor</b>

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:04.430
Nice weather today, huh?

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:06.140
<b>Glare</b>

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:07.350
<i>Awkward.</i>

00:04:08.030 --> 00:04:11.660
<i>It's awkward being stuck in an 
elevator with Port Mafia brass!</i>

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:13.140
<b>A few seconds
 earlier</b>

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:15.140
Hurry! I'm late!

00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:19.120
Nakahara Chuuya-san!

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:19.940
What?

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:21.320
<i>I'm scared...</i>

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.840
<i>But I won't make it if I 
don't get in! Be strong!</i>

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:25.700
What, are you going to leak?

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.450
<b>Silence</b>

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:29.200
Huh?

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:30.960
It seems to have stopped.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:34.320
The buttons aren't working, either.

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:37.210
Has it broken down?!

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:39.450
Ah, I get it.

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:44.600
You may have thought I'm in the 
middle of a mission, Chuuya-san...

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:47.280
I'm just here to hang out!

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:48.870
Free me, please!

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:50.350
What are you talking about, kid?

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:53.820
You aren't using your ability 
to stop the elevator somehow?

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:55.350
Like, hrmphh!

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:55.350
<b>Hrmprhh</b>

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:58.360
That's a really dull excuse 
to blame my ability.

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:01.280
Do you have business at the 
movie theater, too, then?

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:04.120
Yeah, you could say that.

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:07.490
But the only thing that's 
showing here right now...

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:09.240
<b>Movie</b>

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:09.240
<b>The Boy and
 the Puppy</b>

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:11.690
You wouldn't watch that, would you?

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:15.870
W-W-We should focus on getting 
out of this situation.

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:18.640
True. The movie's about to start, too.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:20.120
All right.

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:21.950
Get moving, damn it!

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:24.110
Don't! You're going to break it even more!

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:28.430
Oh, that reminds me of
 something interesting.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:29.260
What?

00:05:29.450 --> 00:05:31.440
You'd think that when an elevator falls,

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:34.630
it's because the wire holding 
it up has failed, right?

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:34.220
<b>Kyaaa</b>

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:39.030
Apparently, it's more common for the floor 
to give out so the passengers fall through.

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:37.520
<b>Aaa</b>

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:42.740
Oh?

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:44.110
The floor, huh?

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:49.160
Chooyah!

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:49.160
<b>Chooyah!</b>

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:52.920
It's not like I moved to the ceiling 
because of what you told me or anything!

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:55.160
I didn't say anything.

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:57.460
I question the common wisdom of the floor.

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:02.430
I will stand only where I so choose, 
so long as I am myself.

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:04.820
He's trying to distract 
me with a cheap poem.

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:07.740
Although, if I really wanted to, 
I could escape at any time.

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:10.170
I'm sure I could, too, but...

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:11.940
Escape!

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:17.970
But then I'd miss the movie.

00:06:18.330 --> 00:06:21.770
I'm trying to contact the others, 
but I can't get through.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:25.060
How is there no commotion about 
the elevator being stuck for so long?

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:27.090
The power's out!

00:06:27.090 --> 00:06:28.200
Stay calm.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:33.010
This isn't a big deal compared 
to what you've been through.

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:34.060
Chuuya-san...

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:37.700
By the way, why are you 
calling me by my first name?

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:39.130
That's what matters right now?

00:06:39.130 --> 00:06:40.930
That's what Dazai-san calls you, so...

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:42.710
It's back.

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:44.450
We're moving!

00:06:44.450 --> 00:06:45.900
Thank goodness.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:46.210
Yeah.

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:48.680
We'll be just in time for the movie.

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:49.730
Yeah.

00:06:50.150 --> 00:06:50.850
Eh?

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:53.150
Hey, it's Atsushi-kun!

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:54.310
And Chuuya.

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:55.360
Dazai-san!

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:56.640
Why are you here?

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:57.920
To watch a movie.

00:06:57.920 --> 00:06:58.840
I bailed on work.

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:00.920
<b>The Boy and the Puppy</b>

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:02.860
<b>Today's showings are canceled 
due to technical difficulties.</b>

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:02.870
The movie's canceled, too,
 though, thanks to the blackout.

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:05.340
I see...

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:09.590
It is, huh?

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:10.770
It's canceled?

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:15.960
Oh, yeah. Chuuya-san, why don't the three 
of us watch it together next time?

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:17.130
The Boy and the Puppy.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:20.190
Hell no!

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:22.300
What?

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:29.210
Yay, the park at night.

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:32.050
It's definitely pretty cool around here.

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:34.780
So, Kunikida-kun...

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:36.670
How about them yukatas?

00:07:36.670 --> 00:07:38.120
Super nouryou, right?

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:39.120
Yay!

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:40.590
Get off me!

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:42.590
Do you even know what "nouryou" means?!

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.980
<b>Nouryou</b>

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:43.980
<b>To escape the heat 
of summer and 
enjoy the cold</b>

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:47.980
<b>Episode 27</b>

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:47.980
<b>The Armed Detective Agency 
Beats the Heat</b>

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:52.960
Nouryou!

00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:57.010
When I heard you scream that at the office, 
I thought your head had finally fried.

00:07:57.010 --> 00:08:00.840
Oh, come on. You're totally 
digging wearing a yukata, too.

00:08:00.840 --> 00:08:02.940
I'm just trying to play along.

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:06.250
It's nice being out in the cold 
with the other members, huh?

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:08.210
The summer's so nice.

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:11.630
Yukatas, fireworks, the beach, 
self-drowning...

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:12.500
Only for you.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:15.340
Don't you think Atsushi-kun 
should be here by now?

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:16.700
Where did he go?

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:18.900
We asked him to buy fireworks.

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:20.350
Guys!

00:08:20.350 --> 00:08:22.570
Speaking of Atsushi...

00:08:22.570 --> 00:08:24.020
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:27.200
I bought fireworks!

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:29.120
Your yukata's falling apart!

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:32.160
You're practically just wrapped in cloth.

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:35.130
I guess this is what happens 
when you run in a yukata.

00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:36.130
No, it isn't!

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:37.010
What are you, a kid?

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:40.030
Anyway, I wanted you guys 
to check out these fireworks.

00:08:40.340 --> 00:08:41.550
What do you think?

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:50.720
They're so pretty.

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:54.540
What's this, Kyouka-chan?

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:55.770
A cat.

00:08:55.770 --> 00:08:56.930
It's a tiger.

00:08:57.630 --> 00:08:58.850
What about this, then?

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:00.050
A crab claw.

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:01.170
It's a bunny.

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:03.810
<b>This is dangerous. 
Please don't do this</b>

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:02.910
Be careful, you two.

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:05.050
They're having so much fun.

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:06.950
I should try it, too.

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:10.570
<b>Megabomb</b>

00:09:06.950 --> 00:09:09.600
Don't swing that around! 
That's way too dangerous!

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:10.570
<b>Seriously, this is dangerous.
 Please don't ever do this</b>

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:15.240
Sparklers, huh, everyone?

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:25.820
How fleeting... a sparkler, like a human life.

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:27.340
<i>So dark...</i>

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:35.800
Why are there rocket fireworks?

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:37.480
Oh, you didn't know?

00:09:37.690 --> 00:09:40.440
There's a fireworks festival by the port.

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:44.480
This place is actually a secret 
front-row seat for the fireworks.

00:09:57.220 --> 00:10:00.740
If I had to go, I'd like to 
go out just as beautifully.

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:04.980
I'd prefer you don't go.

00:10:58.070 --> 00:11:00.970
Please don't say that. Not even as a joke.

00:11:06.880 --> 00:11:08.080
Pretty.
